# function-result-ignored is OFF by default (FP-prone); the sibling
# function-result-ignored.config.json enables it via "enabled": [...] so this
# fixture exercises it. Fires on a bare-statement call to a same-unit function
# (line 17, Compute); must NOT fire when the result is used (line 18 assignment,
# line 20 condition) nor on a procedure call (line 19, DoStuff has no return type).
function-result-ignored 17
!function-result-ignored 18
!function-result-ignored 19
!function-result-ignored 20
